{"id":"chatcmpl-b3c638a2-8c97-4c22-8321-e2d313aace00","object":"chat.completion","created":1795229230,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task demonstrates handling ambiguous medical imaging questions where the provided view (lateral) is inherently limited for determining laterality. The successful strategy involved consulting an expert tool for descriptive analysis, then making a reasoned selection based on anatomical priors (hemidiaphragm position) when definitive evidence was unavailable. The pattern generalizes to any task requiring forced-choice answers under incomplete information.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When the input modality is inherently ambiguous for the question asked, invoke an auxiliary expert/description tool to extract additional discriminative features before committing to an answer.\",\n    \"When forced to choose between mutually exclusive options under uncertainty, apply domain-specific anatomical or structural priors (e.g., typical positional relationships) to bias selection toward the most plausible option.\",\n    \"Recognize when a tool's input requirements (e.g., frontal view) don't match the available data, and route to an alternative tool that can handle the actual input format rather than forcing an incompatible call.\",\n    \"Use the reasoning trace to explicitly document why definitive determination is difficult, then justify the final choice via the strongest available indirect evidence.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging interpretation\": \"Identify the view/modality first; if it cannot directly answer the question, seek secondary descriptive tools and lean on anatomical priors (positional relationships, typical laterality) to disambiguate.\",\n    \"Forced-choice under uncertainty\": \"Enumerate available indirect clues, rank them by reliability, and select the option best supported by the strongest prior rather than defaulting randomly.\",\n    \"Tool orchestration\": \"Match tool capabilities to input format; skip tools requiring incompatible inputs and prefer general-purpose expert/description tools when specialized ones fail.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm whether the input view/modality can directly resolve the question; if not, plan to gather indirect evidence.\",\n    \"Verify the final answer is justified by at least one concrete anatomical or structural prior documented in the reasoning.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":903,"total_tokens":1315,"completion_tokens":412,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":903},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":412}}}